# 🌊 KINEVO WindSurfRules
> Persistent rules for AI-assisted development in the Momentum / KINEVO React Native mobile app.

🧠 CONTEXT
This is a sports partner discovery app built using React Native (Expo), Zustand, React Query, and Supabase. The app is bilingual (EN/FR), location-aware, and follows atomic design with modular architecture.

---

## 1. 🧱 Architecture & Folder Discipline

- ✅ Use Atomic Design in `src/components` (Atoms, Molecules, Organisms, Business)
- ✅ Use domain-driven structure in `src/features/<feature>/`
- ✅ Use services from `src/shared/services/` for all backend/API logic
- ✅ Keep state inside `src/shared/stores/` with Zustand and proper typing
- ✅ Navigation is handled from `src/navigation/` using React Navigation v7
- ❌ DO NOT place business logic inside UI files

---

## 2. 🔤 Internationalization Rules (Bilingual Support)

- ✅ All user-facing text must use `t('translation.key')`
- ✅ Add new keys to `src/shared/utils/i18n.ts`
- ✅ Always provide both English and French
- ❌ Never hardcode text in components

---

## 3. 🎨 Theming & Styling

- ✅ Use theme tokens: `theme.colors`, `theme.spacing`, `theme.typography`
- ✅ No inline styles unless dynamic or conditional
- ✅ Maintain visual hierarchy and consistent spacing
- ✅ Use `theme-aware` props inside all reusable components
- ❌ Never use hardcoded colors, spacing, or fonts

---

## 4. 🧪 TypeScript First

- ✅ Enforce strict types using interfaces from `src/shared/types/`
- ✅ Use `Database['public']['Tables']['table']['Row']` for Supabase types
- ✅ Every store, service, and hook must be typed
- ❌ No `any`, `unknown`, or `implicit` types in production code

---

## 5. 📦 Component Standards

- ✅ Use existing reusable components before creating new ones
- ✅ Place UI-only logic in `src/components`
- ✅ Place feature-specific logic in `src/features/<module>/components`
- ✅ Test new components inside isolated PreviewScreens first
- ✅ Every component must support:
  - Bilingual labels (`t(...)`)
  - Analytics logging via `logEvent(...)`
  - TestID for testing
  - Theme integration

---

## 6. 🔐 Supabase Integration Rules

- ✅ Always use `supabaseClient` from `src/config/supabase.ts`
- ✅ Use row-level security (RLS) in DB policies
- ✅ Never expose auth-sensitive logic in frontend code
- ✅ Use RPC functions for complex filtering (e.g. discovery logic)
- ❌ Do not query or mutate data directly inside components

---

## 7. 📊 Analytics Tracking

- ✅ Every interaction must use `logEvent(...)`
- ✅ Use `Events` enum for standard events
- ✅ Include context in `properties`: { targetUserId, distance, sport }
- ✅ Track modal openings, screen views, filters, swipes, matches
- ✅ Onboarding must track every user decision or error

---

## 8. 🧭 Navigation & Routing

- ✅ Use deep linking structure: `kinevo://discovery`, `kinevo://chat/:id`
- ✅ Navigation param types must be declared in `src/navigation/types.ts`
- ✅ Bottom navigation bar must show badge for new matches or messages
- ✅ Animate screen transitions when navigating modally

---

## 9. 💾 Data Caching & State Strategy

- ✅ Use Zustand for UI state and lightweight user state
- ✅ Use React Query for all server state (queries, mutations, subscriptions)
- ✅ Use infinite scroll / batching when loading large datasets
- ✅ Invalidate queries on user interaction that changes backend state

---

## 10. ⚠️ UX & Error Handling

- ✅ All async logic must use try/catch
- ✅ Show loading indicators while fetching
- ✅ Show fallback UI when error or empty
- ✅ Use `Alert.alert()` or modals for user confirmations
- ✅ Gracefully degrade when permissions (like location) are denied

---

## 11. 🌍 Location-Aware Discovery Rules

- ✅ Use `expo-location` to request and store user lat/lng
- ✅ Onboarding captures location once with user consent
- ✅ Discovery results must be filtered by proximity (Haversine)
- ✅ Profiles missing location must be excluded from distance filtering
- ✅ Use client-side fallback if RPC fails

---

## 12. 🛠️ General Coding Etiquette

- ✅ Use `console.error()` in dev for catching failures (remove in prod)
- ✅ Organize imports by type: react, 3rd-party, local
- ✅ All function names must be camelCase
- ✅ All file names must be kebab-case or PascalCase (if React component)
- ✅ Leave a TODO or FIXME when logic is incomplete

---

## 13. 🧠 AI & Agent Collaboration

- ✅ Always refer to `PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md` before implementing features
- ✅ Before editing files, check for duplicates and existing reusable logic
- ✅ When introducing new DB logic, update Supabase and types accordingly
- ✅ Update the roadmap section when major milestones are completed
- ✅ Update translations and analytics if relevant

